SELECT 'ROADMAP-1: QNFO.REACH ASK-CANONICAL-1: ask.qwav.org declares ask.qwav.tech its canonical host and sitemap',
 'QNFO.REACH; charter pillar reach; doer: qnfo-ai-search via qnfo-code-orchestrator. Measured 2026-11-04: https://ask.qwav.org/ answers with <link rel=canonical href=https://ask.qwav.tech/> and its robots.txt names Sitemap: https://ask.qwav.tech/sitemap.xml, so search engines are told the answer pages belong to ask.qwav.tech, which docs/DOMAINS.md marks as the wrong plane domain (DOMAIN-PLANE-1:ask.qwav.tech). The scout also reports that qnfo.org links Ask to the .tech host (qnfo-gateway, not re-probed). Work in qnfo-ai-search: derive canonical, og:url, the robots Sitemap line and the sitemap locs from one constant that is ask.qwav.org (requests on the .tech host also declare the .org canonical); only after a probe shows https://ask.qwav.org/ and /sitemap.xml answer 200, 301 page routes of ask.qwav.tech to ask.qwav.org, leaving /api paths untouched on both hosts so shared links and clients keep working. Carry the tag ASK-CANONICAL-1 in a comment at the edit. Read the open DOMAIN-PLANE-1:ask.qwav.tech issue first and link this to it rather than duplicating its redirect step. Done: the runtime probe passes and the sitemap lists ask.qwav.org URLs. Failure mode: a redirect loop or lost attribution for links already shared. Source: docs/BLUE-SKY-ROADMAP-2026-11.md section 4 (PROD-02).' || char(10) || char(10) ||
 'code-task: repo=qnfo-workers path=qnfo-ai-search/worker.js' || char(10) ||
 'code-anchor: <link rel="canonical" href="https://ask.qwav.tech/">' || char(10) ||
 'runtime-probe: {"url":"https://ask.qwav.org/robots.txt","status":200,"absent":"ask.qwav.tech"}' || char(10) ||
 'code-probe: {"paths":["qnfo-ai-search/worker.js"],"contains":"ASK-CANONICAL-1"}',
 'session:bluesky-2026-11', 'code', 'medium', 'open', unixepoch() * 1000, unixepoch() * 1000
