 'QNFO.INFRA; charter pillar core; doer: qnfo-ops via qnfo-code-orchestrator. D1 caps a query result at 50 MB from 2026-11-04 (Cloudflare changelog 2026-10-30, read by a scout; REST import and export are exempt). Tables reported near the limit: code_tasks (ctx, about 250 MB) and chatbox_conversations (about 174 MB); papers.body_md is the other fat column. An unbounded SELECT on them now fails with an opaque error. Work in qnfo-ops d1Query: keep a list of fat-column tables and refuse, before running, a SELECT on one of them that has no LIMIT or that selects the fat column without a bound, with an error that names the 50 MB cap and the fix; map the D1 result-too-large error text to a stable code result_too_large so callers and the self-heal loop can recognise it; add a fixture test. Carry the tag D1-RESULT-CAP-1 in a comment at the edit. Then run the same audit over scripts/ and the dashboard for unbounded reads of those columns and list them on this issue. Done: the guard and test are on main and the audit list is recorded. Failure mode: false positives on legitimate bounded reads, so the guard checks only the listed columns and the absence of LIMIT. Source: docs/BLUE-SKY-ROADMAP-2026-11.md section 5 (CF-A-11, CF-B-15).' || char(10) || char(10) ||
 'code-task: repo=qnfo-workers path=qnfo-ops/worker.js' || char(10) ||
 'code-anchor: async function d1Query(env, args) {' || char(10) ||
 'code-probe: {"paths":["qnfo-ops/worker.js"],"contains":"D1-RESULT-CAP-1"}',
 'session:bluesky-2026-11', 'code', 'medium', 'open', unixepoch() * 1000, unixepoch() * 1000
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE title LIKE 'ROADMAP-1: QNFO.INFRA D1-RESULT-CAP-1:%' AND status = 'open');

